<title>SWITZERLAND: Memphis top world air cargo airport Jan-July - ACI.</title>
<headline>Memphis top world air cargo airport Jan-July - ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in January-July this year, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>The airport handled 1,082,231 tonnes of cargo in Jan-July, up 11.2 percent on first half 1995.</p>
<p>Occupying second-place in the ACI table of top cargo-handling airports was Los Angeles with 961,652 tonnes, up 9.1 percent on the previous year's levels.</p>
<p>In third place was Miami, which handled 953,100 tonnes, 7.8 percent up on the first seven months of 1995.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in Jan-July 1996,(Jan-July 1995 ranking) with the volume handled, in tonnes and the percentage change from Jan-July 1995 were as follows:</p>
<p>    1 (1)  Memphis	     1,082,231   up   11.2</p>
<p>    2 (5)  Los Angeles	   961,652   up    9.1</p>
<p>    3 (4)  Miami		   953,100   up    7.8</p>
<p>    4 (3)  New York		914,364   up    1.2</p>
<p>    5 (2)  Tokyo		   906,309   down  5.5</p>
<p>    6 (7)  Hong Kong	     850,524   up    4.5</p>
<p>    7 (6)  Frankfurt	     845,562   up    1.8</p>
<p>    8 (8)  Louisville	    788,289   up    3.1</p>
<p>    9 (10) Seoul		   744,272   up    9.4</p>
<p>   10(16)  Anchorage	     725,104   up   37.7</p>
<p>   11 (9)  Chicago		 695,834   down  0.1</p>
<p>   12(12)  Singapore	     669,784   up    5.0</p>
<p>   13(11)  London Heathrow     651,453   up    1.2</p>
<p>   14(13)  Amsterdam	     633,914   up   10.3</p>
<p>   15(15)  Paris-CDG	     555,204   up    2.9</p>
<p>   16(14)  New York Newark     550,958   up    1.9</p>
<p>   17(17)  Atlanta		 455,784   up    3.3</p>
<p>   18(18)  Dallas F/W	    433,736   down  0.2</p>
<p>   19(19)  Taipei		  427,856   down  1.3</p>
<p>   20 (-)  Dayton		  408,206   up   17.4</p>
